<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11792" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŭcullus</span></b> , i,
		m. (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŭculla</span></b> ,
			ae, f., in eccl. Lat., <i><span class="en">Paul.
				Nol. 21, 389</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hier. Vit.
			Hil. 46</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ennod. Ep. 9, 14</span></i>)
		[root kal-, of cella, clam, 
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλύπτω</span>; cf. culleus], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a covering</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of the head, <i>a cap, hood, fastened to a garment</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 1, 8,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 98, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 3,
			170</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">as a disguise,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					8, 145 al.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of
			the feet, <i><span class="en">Capitol. Pert. 8</span></i>
			dub.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> Of
			merchandise, <i>a conical wrapper</i> or <i>case</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 2, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
